  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "An organization's values are the bedrock of why the company exists, how behavioral norms are defined, and how decisions are made to achieve goals and fulfill the vision. The goal is to communicate and model these values in your behavior, demonstrating commitment to the company's desired ways of working, and guiding the behavior of your team members accordingly.  \n\n### Communicate the company values \n\nHelp team members develop their understanding of the company values by articulating what each one means to them and why it's important to the company's success. Now ask team members to share a story that exemplifies each value. \n\n### Be a good role model \n\nBe self-aware of your behaviors and how your actions are perceived by the team. Find ways to provide concrete examples of the company values in what you say and do. For example, if the company values collaboration, make an effort to connect your team with other teams to find ways of working better together.",
